  "meta": {
    "source": "figma",
    "derivableFromSource": [
      "props.type",
      "props.default",
      "layout",
      "tokens.bindings"
    ],
    "needsReview": [
      "Drawn in SDD Library from this contract (2026-11-09): one COMPONENT_SET per variant value (Button/classic … Button/ghost, #19), 120 variants each (color × size × highContrast × state, plus loading=true only with state=disable). anchors.figma.node is the Section; anchors.figma.sets, each set. Original reading in Radix: anchors.figma.reference.",
      "In SDD Library the axis is called highContrast (without Radix's \"highConstrast\" typo) and default values carry no ✦: the default is the first variant (solid · accent · 2 · false · default · false).",
      "Spinner: 8-blade _spinner helper with opacities 1/8…8/8 and no token (reference drawing, not animated).",
      "loading=true only exists in Figma together with state=disable (144 variants): the loading design inherits the disabled look. In code, decide whether loading should look like disabled.",
      "classic uses two gradient layers (white → transparent) with no variable, and one at 20% on hover. They are not in tokens.",
      "opacity on hover/active (0.88, 0.82, 0.92) is hardcoded in Figma, with no variable. It is the only case where the contract uses opacity; disabled never does.",
      "surface: Figma defines no background for neutral and error colors in default/hover (only accent uses tokens.colors.accent-surface). Radix uses --color-surface.",
      "Figma inconsistencies: text of non-solid variants in accent uses accent-alpha.11, but neutral and error use the solid step 11; in highContrast the text on solid/classic is neutral.1 in accent and neutral, and error.1 in error; classic highContrast with color=error uses accent's shadows; classic disabled uses the button-classic-accent shadow.",
      "ghost uses text-style …regular in size 2 (the other variants, medium). Not verified in size 1, 3 and 4.",
      "Size 1, 3 and 4 tokens were read only in solid + accent + default; they are assumed to hold for the other variants. The focus ring was only read in accent.",
      "Widths: size 2 without icon = 70px; the width depends on the sample text \"Button\".",
      "Do not exist in Figma: fullWidth (removed from the contract), type, onPress.",
      "Contrast and touch target not measured."
    ]
  }
}
